#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do I cite Qiskit in my research? {#how-do-i-cite-qiskit-in-my-research}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cite Qiskit by using the included [BibTeX "
"file](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/CITATION.bib).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do I cite an IBM Quantum computer in my research? {#how-do-i-cite-an-"
"ibm-quantum-computer-in-my-research}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For research papers, we encourage authors to acknowledge IBM Quantum&reg; by"
" using:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
">    We acknowledge the use of IBM Quantum services for this work. The views"
" expressed are those of the authors, and do not reflect the official policy "
"or position of IBM or the IBM Quantum team.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Paper references should use the following citation:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> IBM Quantum. https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com</span>/, YYYY\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum processing units in the paper should be referenced by their unique name (for example, `ibmq_vigo`) and optionally\n"
"adding the version (for example, `ibmq_vigo` v1.0.2).  We also encourage referencing the processor.\n"
"For example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> In this paper we used `ibmq_vigo`, which is one of the IBM Quantum Canary "
"processors.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example of citing an IBM Quantum program:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> IBM Quantum (2025). Estimator primitive (Version x.y.z) [computer "
"software]. https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com</span>/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do I cite IBM Quantum Composer in my research? {#how-do-i-cite-ibm-"
"quantum-composer-in-my-research}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example citation for IBM Quantum Composer:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> IBM Quantum Composer. 2025. url: "
"https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer</span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I don't see something in the user interface, such as my administration "
"tasks. {#i-dont-see-something-in-the-user-interface-such-as-my-"
"administration-tasks}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Try choosing a different account from the account switcher in the header of "
"the [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com) interface.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I'm just using the Open Plan, but I had to put in my credit card.  Will I be"
" charged? {#im-just-using-the-open-plan-but-i-had-to-put-in-my-credit-card-"
"will-i-be-charged}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You will not be charged unless you create a Pay-As-You-Go "
"[instance](/guides/instances) and use it to send workloads to QPUs. See "
"[Manage cost](/guides/manage-cost) for instructions to set a cost limit and "
"to learn about other ways to manage costs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What's the difference between an API key and an API token? {#whats-the-"
"difference-between-an-api-key-and-an-api-token}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's no difference.  The terms API key and API token are used "
"interchangeably. You'll see both terms in the documentation because "
"different interfaces use different terms.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bearer\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What's the difference between an API token and a bearer token? {#whats-the-"
"difference-between-an-api-token-and-a-bearer-token}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An API token is a long-lived credential used to [authenticate to the Qiskit "
"Runtime service](/guides/hello-world#install-and-authenticate).  A bearer "
"token is a temporary credential that is used to [authenticate to the REST "
"API in an untrusted environment](/guides/cloud-setup-untrusted#authenticate-"
"to-the-rest-api-in-an-untrusted-environment).  A bearer token cannot be used"
" to authenticate to the Qiskit Runtime service.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Do I have to choose the region that I live in? {#do-i-have-to-choose-the-"
"region-that-i-live-in}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No. You can use either region.  The region determines where jobs are run and"
" where the data is kept.  Additionally, you can only see and use instances "
"that were created in the instance that you are logged in to. Note that only "
"the us-east region supports the Open Plan.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Can I connect through a proxy server? {#can-i-connect-through-a-proxy-"
"server}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, but you must use Qiskit Runtime v0.44.0 or later.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What is the data retention policy? {#what-is-the-data-retention-policy}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM retains your (undeleted) job and usage data for three years while you "
"continue to use the Qiskit Runtime service.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What happened to Python distributions such as Qiskit Aer, Qiskit Nature, and"
" Qiskit Experiments? {#what-happened-to-python-distributions-such-as-qiskit-"
"aer-qiskit-nature-and-qiskit-experiments}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, the command `pip install qiskit` "
"will **only** install the [Qiskit SDK](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit). "
"This means that some modules that you have used in the past, such as "
"`qiskit-aer` or `qiskit-nature`, now have to be installed separately.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, Qiskit was comprised of many "
"different Python distributions, such as `qiskit-terra`, the compiler core; "
"`qiskit-aer`, the high-performance simulator; the original IBM Quantum&reg; "
"provider; and several now-obsolete packages providing particular exploratory"
" algorithmic or experiment-running features.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These separate software packages were combined into what was called the "
"Qiskit *metapackage*, which allowed users to install all of these components"
" together through `pip install qiskit`. This metapackage architecture was "
"removed with the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, and now each of the "
"individual software distributions needs to be installed separately.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you want to install the packages that were previously included in the "
"Qiskit metapackage, visit the [Qiskit "
"ecosystem](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/ecosystem) to find a range of "
"packages to suit your needs. You can also read the [v1.0 migration "
"guide](/guides/metapackage-migration) for more information about this "
"change.\n"
msgstr ""

